---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import RollingAverageCalculator from "../../components/calculators/RollingAverageCalculator";

const seo = {
  page_description: "Calculate the rolling average of your daily metrics to understand long-term trends.",
  open_graph_type: "website"
};
---
<Layout seo={seo} title="Rolling Average Calculator | TrackAndLog">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Rolling Average Calculator</h1>
      <p>A rolling average smooths out daily fluctuations (variance) in your data to reveal the underlying trend. Enter your data below to see how a rolling window affects your average.</p>

      <noscript>
        <div class="bg-gray-100 p-4 border border-gray-300 my-4">
          <p><strong>JavaScript Required</strong></p>
          <p>This calculator requires JavaScript to run interactively. The mathematical formula for a rolling average of window size <em>n</em> is:</p>
          <code>Average = (Sum of last n days) / n</code>
        </div>
      </noscript>

      <RollingAverageCalculator client:load />

      <h2>Why use a rolling average?</h2>
      <p>If you weigh yourself daily, your weight will fluctuate based on hydration and time of day. Looking at a 7-day rolling average provides a truer picture of your <a href="/metrics/weight">weight</a> trajectory.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
